fix(i18n): the Hungarian retry line stops saying the duration is what keeps trying

`"Összesen {duration} próbálkozik tovább."` renders as "Összesen 2 perc próbálkozik tovább", which reads as "a total of
2 minutes keeps trying": the duration lands in the subject slot. Adding the postposition (`ideig`) is what marks it as
a span of time.

English is unchanged, so every `@key.sourceHash` stays valid and nothing needs restamping.

The rule behind it goes in `docs/i18n/hu/glossary.md`, because it is not about this key: English marks the role with a
preposition (`for a total of {duration}`), while the Hungarian placeholder arrives as a bare nominative phrase ("2
perc") that can't be inflected, since nothing knows which word is in it. A postposition after it is the only way to say
"for this long", and a bare duration placeholder is wrong every time.
